codex
The fixed semantics’ integer floor-division rule expands to symbolic `%Int`, and the backend cannot decide the nonlinear remainder term—it repeatedly retries the built-in `%Int` simplifier. I’m switching to the straightforward summation loop. This removes symbolic division from program execution and enables the Kit’s intended loop-circularity proof against a closed-form triangular-number summary.
apply patch
