codex
The bounded traces identified the issue cleanly: after one iteration the semantics recurs at internal `#while(...)`, while my invariant started at source `While(...)`. Because those shapes differ, the circularity never applies and the prover unrolls. The Kit’s circularity guidance requires anchoring on the stable internal loop head, so I’m changing only that claim boundary.
